2026-08-13,Rublon,PHP Laravel Developer (Cybersecurity),Traffit,https://justjoin.it/job-offer/rublon-php-laravel-developer-cybersecurity--krakow-php-78ef2dab,SUBMITTED,"Traffit green-check thank-you page (rublon.traffit.com/public/form/thankyou/72). Traffit renders a checkmark rather than text, same as the Pretius confirmation on 13 Aug.",100-120 PLN/h net,no,"SUBMITTED 15 Aug, after being stuck as a hand-back since 13 Aug. THE BLOCKER IS SOLVED: the Country/City widgets that 'kept clearing each other' are custom searchable dropdowns where the <select> is an empty proxy and the real control is a text input with placeholder 'Start typing to find location.' - you must click it, type a PARTIAL term, then CLICK the rendered option. Country: type 'Ital' -> pick 'Italia'. City: type 'Venez' -> pick 'Venezia, Venezia, Veneto'. Reached via the justjoin Apply button, which opens the EXTERNAL Traffit form in a new tab and therefore BYPASSES the justjoin reCAPTCHA entirely. Answers, all truthful: preferred work type = Business contract (B2B); expected rate = 'EUR 250-300 per day (B2B, excl. VAT)'; available = 'In 2 weeks' (closest option to his 1 Sep date, same choice as Pretius); 'Do you live in the EU and have a work permit?' = YES; 'Would you work at an office if available in your location?' = 'No, 100% remote work' (chosen because any office answer would assert a commuting commitment to Poland he has not made); 'Do you speak Polish fluently?' = NO (honest, and likely a screen-out risk on a Polish employer). Canonical CV attached, both GDPR consents ticked. Role: Laravel 12 / PHP 8.3, AI-agent tooling, GitHub-based CI/CD, degree clause is 'formal education OR equivalent experience', PLN 15,000-23,500/mo."
