2026-08-16,BeReal.,QA Automation Engineer,LinkedIn / own ATS,https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4444978121/,DROPPED - native French required,not applied,,no,"QA Automation title and remote-listed, so it looked promising, but the ad requires 'Native or Bilingual equivalent level in both French' and the work is mobile automation on a high-volume consumer app rather than his web/API Playwright profile."
2026-08-16,Tavily (Nebius Group),Technical Support Engineer,Greenhouse,https://job-boards.eu.greenhouse.io/tavily/jobs/4877911101,SUBMITTED,"Thank you for applying. Your application has been received. If there is a fit, someone will be getting back to you.","USD 109,000-136,000",no,"SUBMITTED, confirmation page reached. BEST PAY of any role applied to: USD 109,000-136,000 base, Remote - Europe (also US/Tel Aviv; offices Amsterdam, Tel Aviv, NYC, Austin). Asks exactly 2+ years technical support in B2B, NO degree clause. The JD reads like his CV: Python, LLM toolchains (LangChain/LlamaIndex/vector DBs), RAG, prompt engineering, agent architectures, API and third-party integration troubleshooting, and it names N8N explicitly - the tool he uses daily at FlowSpace. Answers: Venice, Venezia, Italy / country Italy / LinkedIn given / read Nebius Candidates Privacy Policy = Yes / languages = English + Italian (Hindi is NOT in their fixed list) / authorized without sponsorship = Yes / reside in the location specified = Yes (role is Remote-Europe and he is in Italy) / previously employed by Nebius = No. GDPR 720-day data-retention consent left UNCHECKED. NOTE: Tavily was acquired by Nebius Group in Feb 2026, and Nebius sits on the do-not-repeat tab for a DIFFERENT req that was blocked by a US-states-only residence dropdown - not a rejection - so this was not treated as a duplicate."
2026-08-16,Crossover (Trilogy),Technical Support Engineer,Crossover platform,https://www.crossover.com/roles/a0s0o00000NhIKdAAN/technical-support-engineer/apply,ACTION_REQUIRED,not submitted,,no,"WORTH HIS TIME. USD 60,000/yr, fully remote, listed for Bologna Italy, and the JD describes his actual work almost line for line: replicating issues, analysing logs, tracing API interactions, reading JSON payloads, 'distinguishing a 401 from a 404 from a 429', and leveraging AI aggressively without trusting it blindly. NO years bar and NO degree clause. Blocked because the apply page offers only 'Apply with Google' or 'Apply with LinkedIn' - OAuth account creation, which I do not do. Be aware Crossover's process is famously assessment-heavy (cognitive test plus role-specific assessments), so budget real time rather than treating it as a quick CV drop. | [2026-08-24] Application about to expire (Aug 23)"
2026-08-16,Quik Hire Staffing (reposting micro1),"Support Engineer (Remote, contract)",micro1.ai,https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4454874728/,NEEDS YOU - account + AI interview,not submitted,,no,"Remote work-from-anywhere contract, USD 25-50/hour, SaaS support via chat and email, no years bar, English only. Top of that band (~EUR 370/day) clears his B2B floor; the bottom (~EUR 185/day) does not, so rate is negotiable ground. Two things to know: 'Quik Hire Staffing' is not the employer, it is REPOSTING a micro1.ai listing with its own referral code attached, and micro1 requires creating an account and sitting an AI-conducted interview. I cannot create accounts, so this one is his if he wants it."
2026-08-16,Jobgether (partner co) / knowmad mood / Capitole,Automation Specialist n8n Expert; Architect AI & Automation n8n x3; AI Automation Engineer n8n,LinkedIn,https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4452702191/,DROPPED - n8n lane is country-fenced,not applied,,no,"GROUPED, and worth knowing as a pattern: a dedicated n8n keyword sweep of the EU (2-week window, remote filter) returned SEVEN hits and every single one is closed to him on geography or level, even though n8n is his single strongest differentiator. Jobgether Automation Specialist (n8n Expert) is Easy Apply and a perfect skills match but states the partner company wants someone ""based in Belgium"". knowmad mood Architect AI & Automation (n8n, IA Generativa, Multiagentes) x3 is Spain-only, Spanish-language titled, and Architect-grade (over-level). Capitole AI Automation Engineer is explicitly ""100% Remote From Spain"". n8n the company itself posted only a Senior Product Security Engineer (senior + security, wrong lane) and a Global Director of Revenue Enablement. CONCLUSION: the EU n8n market is currently hiring residents of Spain and Belgium, not remote-from-Italy. Revisit when a Remote-EU or Remote-Italy n8n req appears."
2026-08-16,Harvey,Integration Engineer; Automation Engineer Customer Education,Ashby,https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/harvey/b0d9328e-04a3-4d83-ba43-237d4026c339,"DROPPED - US-remote, not EU",not applied,,no,"Surfaced by a direct Ashby API sweep of 50 AI/LLM company slugs as the only two title-and-keyword matches. Both are tagged 'Remote' but are US roles: sibling reqs are New York and San Francisco, comp is quoted in USD (133.5K-200.3K and 123.6K-185.4K), and there is no EU/EMEA location option. Recorded so the same two roles are not re-checked next sweep."
2026-08-16,Veeva Systems,Implementation Consultant - Commercial (Vault CRM),Lever,https://jobs.lever.co/veeva/00106429-e952-4ebb-b56f-b8ea57e58f6d,INTERVIEWING,not submitted,,no,"BEST OF THIS ROUND and worth him finishing. Posted as ITALY - MILAN, listed Remote, 'Work Anywhere' policy, and the ad says the role is ideally near a Veeva office (Barcelona, London, Paris, Frankfurt, Berlin, Milan, Budapest) but 'other EU locations will be considered' - Venice is fine. Asks '3+ years of consulting experience OR EQUIVALENT EXPERIENCE', which is exactly the equivalence escape valve that gets past his Philosophy BA, and NO degree clause. Fluent English is the only language requirement; I checked and the 'Additional European language (French, German, Spanish, or Italian)' line sits under Nice to Have, not Requirements. TWO REASONS I STOPPED: (1) a REQUIRED radio asks 'Are you a legally protected status person (according to Law 68/1999)?' - that is Italian protected-category/disability law and only he knows the answer, I will not guess at personal status data; (2) the form also carries hCaptcha. ANSWER SHEET for the rest: Full name Prabhavit Gupta / prabhavitg@gmail.com / +39 351 610 7807 / Current location 'Venice, Italy' / LinkedIn https://www.linkedin.com/in/prabhavit/ / CV Prabhavit_CV.pdf / marketing-contact box leave UNCHECKED. Note their process adds a third-party personality assessment and a practical case exercise AFTER the application. | [2026-08-24] Next Steps email received (Aug 21)"
2026-08-16,Canonical,Cloud Support Engineer; Associate Linux Support Engineer,Greenhouse,https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/canonical/jobs/6448444,NEEDS YOU - anti-AI attestation + essay,not submitted,,no,"Globally remote with NO country fence, and the degree clause has an escape ('or a compelling narrative about your alternative chosen path'), so on paper both are open to him and the Associate role matches his years. HANDED BACK for the reason we always hand back: the form requires a written narrative justifying his HIGH SCHOOL performance, plus a signed attestation 'I agree to use only my own words... use of AI... will disqualify my application'. An AI filling that form is precisely what they are screening out, so he writes it or nobody does. Separately, both roles want real OpenStack/Kubernetes/Linux infrastructure depth, which is a genuine stack stretch, not just a paperwork issue."
2026-08-16,Hire Feed / Quik Hire Staffing / FetchJobs.co / Crossing Hurdles,Reposted 'EU Remote' engineering and QA roles,LinkedIn reposters,https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4455170454/,DROPPED - reposters funnelling to account-gated platforms,not applied,,no,"PATTERN, not a single role. LinkedIn's EU-remote results are now dominated by reposter accounts that are not the employer. Every one traced to a platform requiring account creation and vetting: Hire Feed's 'Software Engineer - Evaluation' goes to work.turing.com (and the body actually asks for a SENIOR Go engineer, not the advertised title); Quik Hire Staffing goes to micro1.ai with its own referral code attached; Crossing Hurdles offers USD 15.3/hr for Italian-language AI QA, far below his floor and needing fluent Italian. Treat any listing from these accounts as an account-gated dead end and skip on sight."
