2026-08-17,Paperpile,"Full-Stack Engineer (TypeScript, React)",Workable,https://jobs.workable.com/view/1s7uaR9JntM1WFge5TbFNp,NEEDS YOU - required cover letter + project essay,not submitted,,no,"Genuinely open on every hard filter, which is rare: NO years bar, NO degree clause, NO language requirement, pay EUR 60,000-90,000 above his band, and the ad says 'distributed team across six countries' and 'work from anywhere on your own schedule', so the Austria tag is where they are, not a residency gate. Playwright is named directly in the requirements. HANDED BACK because the form requires TWO written pieces: a cover letter whose label reads 'Just a few personal sentences. Please no AI boilerplate, it's your chance to stand out', and 'Tell us briefly about a challenging project you worked on the frontend and backend'. The cover letter explicitly rules out AI-written text, so he writes both or nobody does. The rest is easy if he does: total years in software = 3, professional React frontend years, professional backend TypeScript years, address, CV. Stretch to be aware of: they want deep production React and pixel-perfect Figma delivery, which is his weakest area."
