2026-08-17,Cleeng / Softeta / EveryPay / Optasia / MORO Technology / Infoquest / Workato / AIRS Medical / Inspired Thinking / Phoenix Software / Ali Professional,"Fresh QA, support, integration and PHP reqs (11 companies)",Workable + Greenhouse,https://jobs.workable.com/view/onJdfYEDNvJLxMVves4Dpp,DROPPED - all 11 killed on hard filters,not applied,,no,"MORNING SWEEP 17 Aug, grouped. A paced re-harvest of the recovered Workable API plus Greenhouse produced ~99 unique fresh postings; after dedupe against the 993-name set, 11 new companies were verified live against their own JSON-LD (applicantLocationRequirements, jobLocationType) and full requirements text. EVERY ONE died. PER-COUNTRY GEO-FENCING was the dominant kill and it is worth seeing the pattern: Cleeng advertises '100% remote outside Poznan' in its marketing copy but its JSON-LD says Poland ONLY; Softeta is a perfect Playwright+TypeScript stack match at EUR 2,700-3,500/mo but Lithuania only; EveryPay and Optasia are Greece only; MORO is Belgium only AND wants a BSc/MSc in CS with no equivalence clause. Others: Ali Professional posted two Italy roles (Rome on-site PHP, Milan AI fullstack with full-remote possible) but BOTH job descriptions are written entirely in Italian; Infoquest is an exact PHP/Laravel/Vue match in Brescia but asks 5+ years; Workato Forward Deployed Engineer is UK-only-no-sponsorship plus a degree bar plus 4+ years; AIRS Medical names Italy explicitly but requires fluent English, Italian AND French; Inspired Thinking and Phoenix Software both say 'Remote' while their JSON-LD says United Kingdom only. LESSON: marketing copy lies about remote scope - read applicantLocationRequirements in the JSON-LD, not the prose."
